<br/> <br/>An image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Sorry Marcel this one doesnt work for me. I have to agree with one of your commenters, there needs to be a sense of placement where this part of a larger scene such as wall mural with additional street scene if that is indeed the case. It actually feels like some bizarre PS filters have been used to transform a normal image which is a long way from my interpretation of the challenge theme.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An image that does not meet the challenge Sorry Marcel this one doesnt work for me. I have to agree with one of your commenters, there needs to be a sense of placement where this part of a larger scene such as wall mural with additional street scene if that is indeed the case. It actually feels like some bizarre PS filters have been used to transform a normal image which is a long way from my interpretation of the challenge theme.', '2017-05-08 12:04:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(7512579, 1199350, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>This certainly fits the challenge theme. I like the way the bins are also a part of the larger graffiti mural. Compositionally I think I would have tilted the camera to exclude the sky and roof furniture it doesnt add anything whereas more street foreground would help contain and concentrate the focus more</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge This certainly fits the challenge theme. I like the way the bins are also a part of the larger graffiti mural. Compositionally I think I would have tilted the camera to exclude the sky and roof furniture it doesnt add anything whereas more street foreground would help contain and concentrate the focus more', '2017-05-08 12:08:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7512581, 1199071, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>Another great entry Gin Tay, this is a lovely piece of work, the subject is really appealing and very well done. I may have cropped the left at the end of the painting to give more of an impression of a larger continuous work as you have on the right.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge Another great entry Gin Tay, this is a lovely piece of work, the subject is really appealing and very well done. I may have cropped the left at the end of the painting to give more of an impression of a larger continuous work as you have on the right.', '2017-05-08 12:15:02.000000', NULL, 0),
